# HuntMatmulExperts-4 (new, bit-identical): a MoE layer's router K-slice sum (_router_sum) folded into the top-k
# (glue._topk_sum: each row's logits summed over the 8 slices in slice order, then _topk line for line), so routing
# is _router_part + one kernel instead of three kernels, and the fp32 logits never round-trip through memory (b.mlog
# is read by nothing else). 42 launches a verify window and prompt chunk less. Bits: test_route_sum.py (sm_120): picks
# and weights equal the stock pair at rows 1-33, 48, 64, 100, 2,048, 4,096, ties included (zero rows: lowest ids),
# the logits buffer left unwritten; TF_GLM_ROUTE_SUM=0 runs the stock pair. Laptop (RTX 5070, CUDA graph, 8 router
# copies, interleaved medians): -0.55 to -1.0 us a layer (-9 to -13%) at 1-32 rows. GB10 estimate ~1 us a MoE layer =
# ~40 us a window (0.04-0.15%), unmeasured.
